  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThis project involves developing a system for analyzing the U-tube dynamical system to identify legal states. The U-tube dynamical system is represented through various attributes and states, which need to be understood to determine their legality.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective is to learn and establish rules that accurately identify legal states within the U-tube system. This requires analyzing different state attributes and classes.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Researchers and Engineers: Individuals who study dynamical systems and require accurate models for simulations.\n- Data Scientists: Professionals who analyze data to improve the understanding of the U-tube system.\n- System Developers: Engineers responsible for implementing and maintaining the software.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- State Analysis: The system should analyze and categorize states of the U-tube system using attributes such as `value1`, `value2`, and `direction`.\n- Rule Learning: Develop algorithms to derive rules for identifying legal states based on analyzed data.\n- Database Management: Efficient handling and query processing of U-tube states and their attributes within the database.\n- Integration and Update: Ability to update state data and rules as new data is collected and analyzed.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: The system should process states and rules efficiently, with a minimal response time for database queries.\n- Scalability: Ability to handle an increasing volume of state data as the system evolves.\n- Reliability: Ensure accuracy in state classification, minimizing errors in legal state identification.\n- Maintainability: Provide easy updates and maintenance of system components as new insights and data become available.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0137\nCREATE TABLE `utube_state` (\n  `state_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `value1` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `value2` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `direction` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `is_legal` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`state_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `utube_rule` (\n  `rule_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `rule_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `condition_expression` text NOT NULL,\n  `is_active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`rule_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `state_rule_evaluation` (\n  `evaluation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `state_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rule_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `matched` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`evaluation_id`),\n  KEY `state_rule_evaluation_ibfk_1` (`state_id`),\n  KEY `state_rule_evaluation_ibfk_2` (`rule_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `state_rule_evaluation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`state_id`) REFERENCES `utube_state` (`state_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `state_rule_evaluation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`rule_id`) REFERENCES `utube_rule` (`rule_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
